    {
      "date": "2026-07-16",
      "description": "Gas prices rise, national average reaches $3.94/gallon.",
      "details": "The national average for a gallon of regular gasoline increased by 10 cents from the previous week, reaching $3.94. This rise was attributed to instability along the Strait of Hormuz, pushing crude oil prices towards $80 per barrel. Higher gas prices typically reduce discretionary spending, leading to suppressed ROAS and increased CPA for non-essential goods like specialty food.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "AAA Fuel Prices"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-21",
      "description": "TikTok 'Give Me 10' trend goes viral.",
      "details": "The 'Give Me 10' trend, originating from the reality show Love Island, gained significant traction on TikTok. Creators used an audio clip to react to moments of pressure or decision-making, signaling a need for '10 minutes' to cool down or think. Viral trends like this can increase engagement on social platforms but divert user attention from product discovery, potentially leading to lower conversion intent and thus suppressed ROAS and higher CPA.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "feed",
      "icon": "📱",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "Drizzle Digital, Influential"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-23",
      "description": "National average gas price jumps 15 cents to $4.09/gallon.",
      "details": "The national average for regular gasoline surged by 15 cents in one week, reaching $4.09 per gallon, with most states now averaging $4 or higher. This spike was driven by rising crude oil prices and continued volatility along the Strait of Hormuz, pushing crude into the $90 per barrel range. Such a significant increase in a visible cost-of-living expense like gas can heighten consumer financial anxiety, leading to reduced discretionary spending and negatively impacting ROAS and CPA.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "AAA Newsroom"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "description": "Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index falls to 90.8 in July.",
      "details": "The Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index decreased by 1.4 points to 90.8 in July, down from an upwardly revised 92.2 in June. The Expectations Index remained unchanged at 74.7, staying below the 80.0 threshold historically associated with recession risk since February 2025. This sustained pessimism about future economic conditions can lead consumers to pull back on discretionary purchases, negatively affecting ROAS and increasing CPA for premium brands.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "The Conference Board, PR Newswire"
    },
    {
